codex
The typed-head split still left a non-integer symbolic branch because K’s subsort test remains a path predicate rather than a constructor refinement. I’m replacing that encoding with an inductive `IntVals` verification datatype and a total erasure into the semantics’ ordinary `ValSeq`. This is an isomorphic representation of every finite `List[int]`, gives the prover genuinely typed heads, and avoids adding behavior to the Python semantics.
apply patch
